# Pin legacy-ledger migration SQL files to CRLF line endings.
#
# Why: sqlx records a SHA-384 checksum of each migration file's raw bytes in
# the _sqlx_migrations table when first applied. Our production legacy DB
# (bb-vault-legacy-db) was populated by the original blind4 build (2026-04-16),
# which was checked out with CRLF line endings on the build host. If a later
# build checks out the same files with LF endings, sqlx computes a different
# checksum and refuses to start with:
#   "migration 20231208110808 was previously applied but has been modified"
#
# Forcing CRLF on these files keeps every future build byte-identical to what
# the live DB recorded. Do not relax this without also re-stamping the
# _sqlx_migrations.checksum column on every legacy DB in existence.
legacy/the-ledger/migrations/*.sql text eol=crlf
legacy/examples/rust/migrations/*.sql text eol=crlf
